(7243458, 1123245, 101668, '<td valign="top">Ewes often abandon their twins in winter. Their herder gathers these abandoned lambs and rears them by hand. That is why there are sheep in the background and the title.</td>', 'Ewes often abandon their twins in winter. Their herder gathers these abandoned lambs and rears them by hand. That is why there are sheep in the background and the title.', '2014-07-23 03:11:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7243473, 1123212, 147314, '<td valign="top">Yes Paul, I think the processing is the reason for the low score here. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I think it  would be a 5 max (because when the image is DMC, I almost never give lower than 5). I think you can do better ;-)</td>', 'Yes Paul, I think the processing is the reason for the low score here. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I think it  would be a 5 max (because when the image is DMC, I almost never give lower than 5). I think you can do better ;-)', '2014-07-23 04:40:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(7243474, 1123278, 118154, '<td valign="top">Still I enjoy this.</td>', 'Still I enjoy this.', '2014-07-23 04:50:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7243475, 1123212, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> Yes Paul, I think the processing is the reason for the low score here. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I think it  would be a 5 max (because when the image is DMC, I almost never give lower than 5). I think you can do better ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Kees for your honest feedback. I can see the processing looks pretty rough - unfortunately it looked OK when I submitted it - guess I was working late and too tired or drunk:)</td>', 'Originally posted by Kroburg: Yes Paul, I think the processing is the reason for the low score here. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I think it  would be a 5 max (because when the image is DMC, I almost never give lower than 5). I think you can do better ;-)   Thanks Kees for your honest feedback. I can see the processing looks pretty rough - unfortunately it looked OK when I submitted it - guess I was working late and too tired or drunk:)', '2014-07-23 04:54:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7243477, 1123212, 147314, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by P-A-U-L:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> Yes Paul, I think the processing is the reason for the low score here. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I think it  would be a 5 max (because when the image is DMC, I almost never give lower than 5). I think you can do better ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Kees for your honest feedback. I can see the processing looks pretty rough - unfortunately it looked OK when I submitted it - guess I was working late and too tired or drunk:) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sometimes it happens, you have an image, you edit it, you like it and submit it. And when it is in voting (and you see the scores) you think, what have I done, the processing is so way off. But sometimes you''re so focused on the processing, you can''t take distance and have a proper look.<br/>And when this one was the result of drinking, just submit it (with some adjustments) again for this Friday''s challenge :-)</td>', 'Originally posted by P-A-U-L: Originally posted by Kroburg: Yes Paul, I think the processing is the reason for the low score here. I didn''t vote on this challenge, but I think it  would be a 5 max (because when the image is DMC, I almost never give lower than 5). I think you can do better ;-)   Thanks Kees for your honest feedback. I can see the processing looks pretty rough - unfortunately it looked OK when I submitted it - guess I was working late and too tired or drunk:)   Sometimes it happens, you have an image, you edit it, you like it and submit it. And when it is in voting (and you see the scores) you think, what have I done, the processing is so way off. But sometimes you''re so focused on the processing, you can''t take distance and have a proper look.And when this one was the result of drinking, just submit it (with some adjustments) again for this Friday''s challenge :-)', '2014-07-23 05:06:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7243478, 1123212, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kroburg:</b></div><hr/><i> <br/>Sometimes it happens, you have an image, you edit it, you like it and submit it. And when it is in voting (and you see the scores) you think, what have I done, the processing is so way off. But sometimes you''re so focused on the processing, you can''t take distance and have a proper look.<br/>And when this one was the result of drinking, just submit it (with some adjustments) again for this Friday''s challenge :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ha yes too true. I think the problem is doing the processing so last minute and not having a chance to look with a fresh pair of eyes on different devices. Anyway it is all part of the learning curve.<br/> <br/>Lol yes perhaps submitting a really awful image would be a perfect entry for the drinking challenge:) Good idea!</td>', 'Originally posted by Kroburg: Sometimes it happens, you have an image, you edit it, you like it and submit it. And when it is in voting (and you see the scores) you think, what have I done, the processing is so way off. But sometimes you''re so focused on the processing, you can''t take distance and have a proper look.And when this one was the result of drinking, just submit it (with some adjustments) again for this Friday''s challenge :-)   Ha yes too true. I think the problem is doing the processing so last minute and not having a chance to look with a fresh pair of eyes on different devices. Anyway it is all part of the learning curve. Lol yes perhaps submitting a really awful image would be a perfect entry for the drinking challenge:) Good idea!', '2014-07-23 05:15:35.000000', NULL, 0),
